    GREEN [C0 the unmutated copy]

-- C1  THE PORT -- cstyle.bend's buftypes.go accumulates at the HEAD instead of the
        tail, so render_kernel emits the four buffers in REVERSE order. List.append(a,
        A, xs, ys) IS xs ++ ys -- bend2-constraints.md position 1590, and this is that
        rule with a compiler attached.
   copy: tinybendygrad + portexec copied; bin/ references/ tinygrad/ .venv/ symlinked
    planted cstyle.bend: 1 site, 81 -> 81 bytes
         PORT PROTOTYPE : extern void mm(float* restrict data3_4, float* restrict data2_4, float* restrict data1_4, float* restrict data0_4);
         SHIM CALL      : data3_4, data2_4, data1_4, data0_4
    RED   [C1 THE PORT reverses its own emitted buffer order]

