-- C4  THE PORT, on lane A's one-input row kern2 CLANG. Reported because the answer
        was NOT the predicted one: that kernel reads ONE buffer, so reversing its two
        parameters was expected to be a THEOREM, as portexec's stage-2 theorems are.
        It is not. The harness readback address is fixed by POSITION, so the buffer
        that must be read lands on the one that must be written, and word 0 goes to 0.
